From: Stained Glass OS <dev@stained-glass.example>
Subject: msvcp140_atomic_wait: the C++ library's time zone database (__std_tzdb_*)

Microsoft's STL asks msvcp140_atomic_wait for std::chrono's time zone
database; Wine had stubs, and Word ended at start ("unimplemented function
__std_tzdb_get_time_zones"). Windows answers from ICU; here the answers
come from the IANA database the Linux system keeps in /usr/share/zoneinfo:
the zone and link names from tzdata.zi (sorted, each link naming its zone),
a zone at an instant from its compiled TZif file (the 64-bit part), past
its last transition from the POSIX TZ rule it ends with, and the current
zone from /etc/timezone. Offsets and ranges are in milliseconds, as the
library expects; no leap seconds after those the library knows. A name
outside the database (a path) is refused.

Gate: test/tzdb-gate.sh (make test-tzdb), checked against date(1).

--- a/dlls/msvcp140_atomic_wait/tzdb.c
+++ b/dlls/msvcp140_atomic_wait/tzdb.c
@@ -0,0 +1,656 @@
